Lets an app give a map font faces that every font stack falls back to, after
the style's own font faces. A style's font-faces apply only to the fonts they
name, and most styles have none, so a map had no font for the scripts that
glyph PBFs can't shape, such as Myanmar and Devanagari, unless its style named
one. Style::setFallbackFontFaces() takes the font files in the format of a style's
font-faces entry, without a font name, and every style that loads afterwards
uses them where its own faces don't cover a character.
Issue: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/issues/4500
Upstream: not proposed

